cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use this software, code, or experimental results in your
  research, please cite this repository and the associated paper.

title: >-
  Reliability-Aware Multi-View Forensic Evidence Synthesis for
  Network Intrusion Investigation: Code and Experimental Results

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "AlZain"
    given-names: "Mohammed A."

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2026-08-28"

repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/USERNAME/Reliability-Aware-Multi-View-Forensic-Evidence-Synthesis

abstract: >-
  Source code and experimental results for a reliability-aware
  multi-view forensic evidence synthesis framework for network
  intrusion investigation. The framework organizes network-flow
  observations into semantic evidence views and applies Forensic
  Evidence Reliability Fusion (FERF) to combine global evidence
  importance with record-specific integrity, information-quality,
  and temporal-reliability information. The repository includes
  code for dataset preparation, baseline evaluation, multi-view
  analysis, reliability-aware fusion, ablation and evidence
  degradation, cross-dataset validation, repeated cross-validation,
  statistical analysis, computational-efficiency assessment, and
  scalability evaluation. Experimental datasets are not
  redistributed; official dataset sources and preparation
  information are provided separately.

keywords:
  - "digital forensics"
  - "network forensics"
  - "network intrusion detection"
  - "forensic evidence synthesis"
  - "evidence fusion"
  - "multi-view learning"
  - "reliability-aware reasoning"
  - "FERF"
  - "forensic decision support"
  - "machine learning"

